 "script": [
  {"id": "hook", "text": "A Category 5 super typhoon just passed Guam. Where is Champi going next?"},
  {"id": "f1", "text": "The Joint Typhoon Warning Center says Champi became a Category 5 about six hours after passing ten miles south of Guam on Sunday. The Red Cross reports power and water outages, and more than one thousand people used shelters. President Trump approved emergency declarations for the islands."},
  {"id": "f2", "text": "The Philippine weather service says Champi weakened, then regained super typhoon strength on Monday, with sustained winds of one hundred eighty-five kilometers per hour. It expects it to enter the Philippine area on Tuesday, where it would be named Rosal."},
  {"id": "f3", "text": "PAGASA says landfall is unlikely, but heavy rain may reach extreme northern Luzon. The storm could pass closest to Batanes on Friday. It cautions that the track could still shift, and wind warnings may be raised in the north."},
  {"id": "cta", "text": "Will Champi stay offshore of the Philippines? Yes or no?"}
 ],
